                     "topFinding":  "Full pass: the skip gate did not hold because the working tree went from two modified files to five and one is a deployed runtime file. The overnight audit ran the app and captured the network, and found the v0.8.0 cache-bust contract half-broken. Three modules reached only by a static import (src/util/autofit.js, src/util/print.js, src/util/saved-labels.js) are fetched at bare URLs no release ever changes, and three more (src/state.js, src/util/persist.js, data/label-templates.js) are fetched and instantiated twice per load. Re-verified against source this run: six static import statements at render.js:17-18, state.js:18, editor.js:10, migrate.js:12, and util/saved-labels.js:3. The sharp edge is saved-labels.js against saved-labels-ui.js, a tightly coupled pair where the UI half is versioned and the logic half is not, so the next release touching the logic can ship a fresh caller against a cached callee. PROJECT_SPEC.md records the contract nowhere while four source files cite it. Nothing is broken live, the deployed graph is self-consistent, and the drift chain fixed the over-claiming comment at index.html:109-116 the same night. Health holds at 83: architecture and reliability took the hit, the audit loop and queue gained back about the same by having their best day of the series. Two tensions are now past the ADR threshold, the release-trigger question at runsSeen 4 and the icon vestige at 3.",
